  "body": "Stacked on #2951. The parent is a fork branch. Review the [changes above the parent](https://github.com/qsmits/Camcraft/compare/83affaca1bf4920ed07e29bf7c52bf9c48561b80...6b790f4dd6aa0f4e37feeb03bd16b911fb19d664).\n\nUse the actual faces of a convex prismatic punch in the native Agie job. Include the control's rough-pass corner reach and the wire radius when checking the stock. Compute the separation clearance along the entry face. Keep compensation at the control and preserve the source vertices. A reentrant profile still refuses.\n\nThe original sample uses five straight sides and an oblique 3:4 entry face. The hole is at X-20.5 Y6 and the perpendicular seam is at X-12.5 Y0. The material, wire, stock thickness and QN2 settings are the same as in #2951.\n\nRun the example using a new POLY20 destination:\n```sh\ncargo run -p camcraft-app --bin camcraft-cli -- script examples/agie/oblique-punch.camscript\n```\n\nOn 4c715164b the quick gate passed all 84 post tests. Seven application suites passed another 52 tests. Strict all-targets Clippy passed for camcraft-post. The heavy plan selected 199 app steps. Those steps have not run for this draft.\n\nThe CLI preserved the original rectangular output byte for byte. On the oblique job it preserved all nominal vertices and the hole position. A tight acute corner and a separation or lead shorter than 3 mm produced a refusal and no output directory. Head 6b790f4dd handles a perpendicular foot between five-decimal grid points. The post keeps the hole fixed and selects an exterior point within 0.00001 mm of the true foot. It checks both split lengths and the approach using the emitted coordinates. It refuses a near-limit face if a valid grid point cannot preserve the required clearances. On the final head all 86 native post library tests and strict all-targets Clippy passed. The control plotted SLOPE20, a 7:10 face, with the four expected exterior offsets and a 1 mm final section.\n\nPinning tests: oblique_punch_preserves_nominal_vertices_and_perpendicular_seam and an_acute_miter_needs_more_stock_than_a_round_corner. The offline control imported the unchanged CamCraft POLY20 files. FORMALCHECK reported zero errors and listed setup, reference and option 131072 warnings. GRAFICHECK plotted all five exterior faces. Their straight-face offsets were 0.245, 0.155, 0.140 and 0.134 mm for the rough and three trims. The rough-pass 1 mm separation section followed the oblique face from X-12.696 Y0.147 to X-12.096 Y0.947. The control returned to the original hole at X-20.5 Y6. Stock was Z-20 to Z0. No physical machine cut was made.\n\nEffort: high\nChangelog: The native Agie wire post accepts convex prismatic punches with straight oblique sides. It checks the corner and separation clearances before writing the job.\n\nFixes #2953\n",
